  </div>
  <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 50px; font-weight: bold;">
    Do Not Cut or Separate Forms on This Page — Do Not Cut or Separate Forms on This Page
  </div>
</div>
<div class="page">
  <div style="padding: 20px;">
    <div class="section-header">Instructions for Beneficiary</div>
    <p>The information on Form 5498-QA is furnished to you by the issuer of your Able Life Experience (ABLE) savings account. Form 5498-QA reports contributions, rollovers, and program-to-program transfers to your ABLE account.</p>
    <p><strong>Note:</strong> The information on Form 5498-QA is for informational purposes only. It is not a tax document.</p>
    <p>Box 1. Shows the summary of contributions made to this ABLE account in 2022. In addition, all contributions and Qualified Tuition Plan (QTP) contributions are reported in Box 1. Box 1 also shows the total amount of rollovers to this ABLE account from another ABLE account for the benefit of the named beneficiary or of an eligible individual who is a member of the beneficiary's family who is eligible to have an ABLE account.</p>
    <p>Box 2. Shows the amount of any rollover or program-to-program transfer made to this ABLE account from another ABLE account in 2022. This amount is reported in Box 2. If the rollover or transfer is from another ABLE account for the benefit of the named beneficiary or of an eligible individual who is a member of the beneficiary's family who is eligible to have an ABLE account, the amount is reported in Box 2.</p>
    <p>Box 3. May show the cumulative amount contributed since the account was opened. This amount is reported in Box 3. The cumulative amount is designated beneficiary that was rolled over, or directly transferred (in a program-to-program transfer) to the current ABLE account.</p>
    <p>Box 4. Shows the fair market value of the ABLE account as of December 31, 2022. Box 4 also shows the cumulative amount contributed since the account was opened, if applicable.</p>
    <p>Box 5. The ABLE account was opened in 2022 if the box is checked. If the box is not checked, the account was opened in a prior year.</p>
    <p>Box 6. Eligibility established under Section 529A(a)(1)(A), SSA Title XVI, SSA Title XII, or SSA Title XIX.</p>
    <p>Box 7. Code indicating the type of disability certification under Section 529A(b)(1)(B). See the instructions for the specific code.</p>
    <p><strong>Future developments.</strong> For the latest information about developments related to Form 5498-QA and its instructions, such as legislation or regulatory changes, see www.irs.gov/Form5498QA.</p>
    <p><strong>Free File Program.</strong> Go to www.irs.gov/FreeFile to see if you qualify for no-cost online federal tax preparation, e-filing, and direct deposit or payment options.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="page">
  <div style="padding: 20px;">
    <div class="section-header">Instructions for Issuer</div>
    <p>To complete Form 5498-QA, use:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The 2022 General Instructions for Certain Information Returns, and</li>
      <li>The 2022 Instructions for Form 5498-QA.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To get or to order these instructions, go to www.irs.gov/EmployerForms.</p>
    <p><strong>Filing and furnishing.</strong> For filing and furnishing instructions, including due dates, and requesting filing</p>
    <p style="margin-top: 20px;">or furnishing extensions, see the 2022 General Instructions for Certain Information Returns.</p>
    <p><strong>Need help?</strong> If you have questions about reporting on Form 5498-QA, call the information reporting customer service toll free at 866-455-7438 or 304-263-8700 (not toll free). Persons with a hearing or speech disability with access to TTY/TDD equipment can call 304-579-4827 (not toll free).</p>
  </div>
</div>